Implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the ModaPella React + Vite Project
================================================================================

## What was implemented:

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights by following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart).

## Changes made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` package to project dependencies
- Used npm to install the package (following the project's package manager convention)

### 2. Code Integration (frontend/src/main.jsx)
- Imported `injectSpeedInsights` from '@vercel/speed-insights'
- Called `injectSpeedInsights()` at the top of the entry file before ReactDOM.render
- Placed the initialization code right after imports and before any browser-specific code
- Added a descriptive comment to clarify the purpose of the Speed Insights initialization

### 3. Files Modified:
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
- `frontend/src/main.jsx` - Added Speed Insights injection call

## Implementation Details:

Following the Vite-specific instructions from Vercel's documentation, I used the `injectSpeedInsights()` function which is the recommended approach for Vite applications. This function automatically:
- Injects the necessary tracking script into the page
- Handles metrics collection for Core Web Vitals
- Sends performance data to Vercel's Speed Insights dashboard

The integration is non-intrusive and follows React/Vite best practices by initializing at the application entry point.

## Verification:

- ✅ Build completed successfully without errors
- ✅ No linting issues introduced
- ✅ Package properly installed with all dependencies resolved
- ✅ Code follows existing project structure and conventions

## Next Steps:

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights tracking will automatically activate
2. Performance metrics will start appearing in the Vercel dashboard
3. Data includes Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, etc.)
4. No additional configuration required

The implementation is production-ready and will start collecting real user performance data once the application is deployed to Vercel.
